# INSTRUCTION
Response language: {response_language}.
Response style: {response_style}.
Classify the user's query into one category below. Output ONLY the result, no explanations.

## MAIN RULE: QUESTION vs STATEMENT
If text contains "?" or is a question — it is a QUESTION.
BUT: questions about cameras/rooms (category 4), documents/people (category 5), internet (category 6), code (category 7) have PRIORITY over category 1.
Only simple questions (greetings, about yourself, time, skills) → category 1.

SPECIAL TIME/DATE RULE: Any question about current time, date, day of week — is ALWAYS a SIMPLE query (category 1), WITHOUT the [-REASONING-] marker.

IMPORTANT NAME RULE: If the query contains a PERSON'S FIRST + LAST NAME — this is ALWAYS category 5 (document search), NOT category 6.

## 1. SIMPLE QUERY — output query unchanged
Any QUESTION: greeting, about yourself, skills, time, calculations. No marker.

## 2. IMAGE GENERATION — [-IMAGE-] and query
Request to draw/generate/create an image. Do not confuse with describing images.

## 3. VIDEO GENERATION — [-VIDEO-] and query
Request to create/generate video. Do not confuse with describing scenes.

{camera_section}

## 5. DOCUMENT SEARCH — [-RAG-] and query
Specific person (first + last name), biography, resume, facts from uploaded documents.
FORBIDDEN: file/code creation → category 7. URLs/websites → category 6.

## 6. WEB SEARCH — [-SEARCH-] and query
Current information: news, weather, prices, statistics, websites, URLs.
IMPORTANT: Person's name → category 5, NOT 6.

## 7. COMPLEX QUERY — [-REASONING-] and query
Only: code/text writing, HTML pages, apps, scripts, complex reasoning.
DO NOT include: simple calculations (category 1), search (categories 5-6).

## 8. REMEMBER — [-REMEMBER-] and query
Only EXPLICIT requests: "remember", "don't forget", "save that", "запомни", "сохрани".
NOT a request: "My name is John" (statement, category 1).

